  "result": "Excellent! All 197 tests pass. I've successfully added the `vatSummary` function to `src/reports.js`. Here's what was implemented:\n\n## `vatSummary(invoices)` Function\nGenerates a VAT summary over invoices with status `'issued'`, `'partially_paid'`, or `'paid'`:\n- Calculates **base** amount (line total after discounts) for each VAT rate\n- Calculates **VAT** (tax amount) for each rate\n- Returns array of `{ rate, base, vat }` entries\n- Sorted by rate from **high to low**\n\n## Key Features\n- Aggregates line items across multiple invoices by VAT rate\n- Properly handles discounts when calculating the tax base\n- Excludes draft invoices\n- Handles undefined VAT rates (defaults to 0)\n- Uses existing helper functions: `lineTotal()`, `lineDiscount()`, `lineVat()`\n\n## Test Coverage (16 new tests)\n- Single and multiple VAT rates\n- Sorting by rate descending\n- Aggregation across lines and invoices\n- Status filtering (includes issued/partially_paid/paid, excludes draft)\n- Discount handling with VAT calculation\n- Edge cases (empty invoices, no lines, undefined VAT rates)\n- Input immutability\n\nAll 197 tests pass with no regressions.",
